  "body": "It happened out of the blue and i cannot log in anymore with my regular user on my homeserver.\r\nIt does not matter if I use the app or the browser after signing in an endless loop is starting for the sync process. When I reload the browsers I get a message \"Cannot connect to homeserver. Retrying...\"\r\n\r\nIn the logfile I can see errors like:\r\n\r\nsynapse.http.server - 84 - ERROR - GET-5265 - Failed handle request via 'SyncRestServlet': <XForwardedForRequest at 0x7f4f3df6eba8 method='GET' uri='/_matrix/client/r0/sync?filter=5&timeout=0' clientproto=\r\n\r\nIt just happens with this one particular (frequently used) user.\r\n\r\nI tried to change the password on the commandline, but apparently it is still accepting the old one.\r\n\r\nThe user account seems broken.\r\nAny idea what's going on here and how to fix it?\r\n\r\nI am using postgre by the way and did an update today. I was hoping to solve it that way.\r\n\r\nThanks in advance.\r\n\r\n",
